{"parentUuid":"a13ac4af-c17a-4ea5-ad39-d4d2d919b587","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14653213 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"13cd87dd-0b6a-4182-9b98-d0a6cec631ca","timestamp":"2026-09-21T00:50:55.921Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14653213 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_cowork","cwd":"/home/claude","sessionId":"f6c49162-7b81-5373-a7c1-f58edfefee41","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"swirling-plotting-octopus"}
{"parentUuid":"13cd87dd-0b6a-4182-9b98-d0a6cec631ca","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfFfgFTLcmnuHobMB2CRM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sire, the fix is live in production, and the 10-second test clip rendered and saved into your own system.\n\n**What I understood:** You wanted Book One, your character images and your scene art in VisionWeaver. You wanted VisionWeaver to turn them into clips, videos and movies, and you wanted to see everything it makes in your own dashboard, in a Higgsfield-style layout. You also asked me to explain what was wrong.\n\n**What was wrong**\n\nThink of VisionWeaver as a restaurant whose kitchen worked but whose dining room was a painted set.\n\n- **Uploads were fake.** The screen showed your pictures, but they never left your browser. The kitchen never saw them.\n- **Image generation had no reference photos.** It sent Runway an empty photo list, and Runway needs at least one, so image requests failed.\n- **Characters weren't saved.** There was one made-up character, and it vanished on refresh.\n- **There was no way to bring in a book.** There was also no button to stitch clips together.\n- **The Higgsfield look was never built into the dashboard.** That repo only contains behind-the-scenes code with no screens, and it was never switched on.\n\nFinished videos were already being saved to your storage. The screen just wasn't showing them well.\n\n**What I changed**\n\n1. **Database.** I added owner fields and privacy rules so your characters and chapters belong to you.\n2. **The behind-the-scenes function** (`visionweaver-studio`, now v24):\n   - It uses your reference photos, and video can start from a character photo.\n   - It can import a book by chapter.\n   - It can save characters.\n   - It can register uploaded files.\n   - It lists all of this back to the screen.\n3. **The dashboard.** It's now a dark studio with four tabs:\n   - **Create:** write a prompt and pick reference photos.\n   - **Books:** import a chapter file and press \"Make clip\" on any chapter.\n   - **Cast:** save characters with photos.\n   - **Library:** everything made, with play, download, retry and a \"Build master\" button that stitches multi-shot videos into one file.\n4. **Proof.** I ran the site build (it passed), merged to production, and rendered the Chapter 1 test clip. It finished and is stored in your system, so it will show in the Library.\n\n**Two things to know**\n\n- **Sign in with `estibancreations@gmail.com`.** That is the account with permission to use VisionWeaver. The Gmail address on this chat is not the one that has it.\n- **Chapter split.** I made the file **Crossroads_Book1_Convergence_chapters.md** (about 88,600 words, 15 chapters). Chapters 1–4 come from headings in your manuscript. Chapters 5–15 have no headings in it, so I placed those breaks by story position, and they need your check. The manuscript also has no Epilogue text, and Chapter 4's table-of-contents title (\"The Will\") doesn't match its body title (\"The Lawyer\"). I used the body title.\n\n**Your turn**\n\n- Upload the .md in the Books tab.\n- Confirm characters from the covers (I have not named anyone from the images yet). My guesses: the man in the suit on cover 1 is Marcus, the purple-bob woman is Jordan, and the woman with locs is Desiree. Victor and the four portrait photos are unnamed.\n- Add each character's photo in the Cast tab so future clips keep the same faces.\n\n**Not done yet:** stitching a whole movie across many chapters, and switching on Higgsfield (it needs its own keys).\n\n**Sources:** Runway. (n.d.). *API reference*. https://docs.dev.runwayml.com. No Wikipedia was used.\n\nFiles are in the session:\n- Crossroads_Book1_Convergence_chapters.md"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":751,"cache_read_input_tokens":239176,"output_token